description:
STG_GRANTS (stage/stage_views.sql ~184) reads g.value:granteeId and g.value:granteeType from each flattened grant, but the actual /v2/grants payload grant objects use memberId + teamId (grantee type is implied by which is non-null), not granteeId/granteeType. Confirmed live: all 3038 grant rows come back with blank GRANTEE_ID and GRANTEE_TYPE, so you can see the permission and artifactType but NOT who each grant is for -- the core of a permissions audit. Actual grant shape:
  {"memberId":"8Uom...","teamId":null,"permission":"edit","inodeType":"folder","grantId":"...","inodeId":"..."}
Fix: map GRANTEE_ID = COALESCE(memberId, teamId), GRANTEE_TYPE = IFF(memberId IS NOT NULL,'member', IFF(teamId IS NOT NULL,'team', NULL)), and surface grantId/inodeType. Verify grantee resolution against STG_MEMBERS/STG_TEAMS live.

Bash 'trap ... RETURN' set inside run_call_with_progress() (deploy.sh) is not scoped to that function -- once set, it re-fires on every subsequent function return up the call stack (cmd_extract returning, cmd_refresh returning, etc.), not just its own return. By the time those outer frames return, the local $tmp variable from run_call_with_progress is out of scope, so 'rm -f "$tmp"' trips set -u: 'deploy.sh: line 322: tmp: unbound variable'. Confirmed via isolated repro:

inner() { local tmp=x; trap 'rm -f "$tmp"' RETURN; }
outer() { inner; }
outer   # -> unbound variable error when outer (not inner) returns

Harmless in effect (temp file already removed by the time it matters) but noisy/scary at the end of every progress-mode refresh -- reported by Mark seeing it at the end of a refresh run. Fix: make the trap self-clearing so it only fires once, e.g. trap 'rm -f "$tmp" 2>/dev/null; trap - RETURN' RETURN -- verified this stops the re-fire in isolation.
